# ui-icons-hub License & Copyright Notice

Last updated: 2026-09-29

## 1. What this site is

ui-icons-hub is an "index + mirror" reference site: we collect SVG icons scattered
across open-source projects and normalize them (unified viewBox, monochrome icons
switched to `currentColor`, deduplicated and chunked) so they are easy to search
and preview. Every icon collected here remains the property of its original
author / project — this site claims no rights over any of them.

## 2. Licensing of the assets (icons / logos / emoji)

The assets themselves have **no single global license**. Always refer to each
upstream project's actual license — the one listed in the "License" column of
the collection table in the README.

This site only includes collections under permissive licenses. The allow-list:

    MIT / MIT-0 / ISC / BSD-2-Clause / BSD-3-Clause / Unlicense /
    Apache-2.0 / CC0-1.0 / CC-BY-3.0 / CC-BY-4.0 / OFL-1.1

Explicitly excluded: copyleft licenses such as GPL / LGPL / AGPL / MPL,
the CC-BY-SA family (share-alike), and any custom license carrying terms like
"no commercial use", "no derivatives", or "no redistribution".
If something was included by mistake, please open an issue — once verified,
the entire collection will be taken offline.

Practical implications:

  * MIT / Apache-2.0 / BSD / ISC / CC0 families: commercial use, modification
    and redistribution are allowed (most require keeping the notice).
  * CC-BY-3.0 / CC-BY-4.0: commercial use and modification are allowed, but
    **attribution of the original author is mandatory**.
  * CC0-1.0 / Unlicense: copyright waived; the material is public domain.
  * OFL-1.1: applies to fonts and their derived icons; free use and
    redistribution are allowed, but the font itself may not be sold standalone.

Even so, brand logos with trademark status remain governed by trademark law in
every jurisdiction. Confirm the usage rights yourself — or obtain permission
from the rights holder — before any commercial use.

## 3. Original work in this project

The parts written by this project itself — the site pages (index.html,
search.js, app-icons/*), the data-pipeline scripts (search index generation,
chunk packing), and the structured metadata derived from them — are released
under the MIT license: free to use, modify and distribute (including
commercially), provided you keep this section of the notice.

## 4. Distribution & disclaimer

Whether you distribute this project as the online site, an offline archive,
a desktop app or a mobile app, you must include this file together with the
complete collection table (the listing in the README), so that downstream
users know exactly where each icon comes from and under which license.

The assets are provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or
implied. If you find infringing material, a mis-labeled license, or anything
that should be taken down, please open an issue — we will verify and act on
it as soon as possible.

## 5. Thanks to upstream

Thanks to the authors and contributors of every upstream icon project. If you
find an icon set useful, go star its official repository — that is the most
direct way to support its authors.
